      ":question/id": "e985e83b-5aa1-543f-bf29-6cbd6f57ccb6",
      ":question/problem": "$\\displaystyle\\int \\left(-t^{4}+5\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t=$\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(-t^{4}+5\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t &= \\int \\left(-t^{4}+5\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= -\\int t^{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}t+5\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= -\\frac{t^{4+1}}{(4+1)}+5\\frac{t^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+C \\\\ &= -\\frac{t^{5}}{5}+5t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
